### 🔴 HIGH — Finding 2: Sensitive Data Exposure (OWASP A02)

**File:** `app.js`, line 15–18  
**Problem:** Email addresses are returned in the API response. Depending on context, this is a **GDPR/privacy concern** and also enables user enumeration. The `/users` endpoint should follow the principle of **least privilege** — only return data the caller actually needs.

```js
// ❌ CURRENT: Exposes PII unnecessarily
{ id: 1, name: 'Alice', email: 'alice@example.com' }
```

**Recommendation:** Strip sensitive fields and use role-based field filtering.

```js
// ✅ FIXED: Only return what is needed; filter based on role
app.get('/users', requireAuth, (req, res) => {
  const users = [
    { id: 1, name: 'Alice', email: 'alice@example.com' },
    { id: 2, name: 'Bob', email: 'bob@example.com' },
  ];

  // Only admins get email addresses
  const sanitized = users.map(({ id, name, email }) => ({
    id,
    name,
    ...(req.user.role === 'admin' && { email }),
  }));

  res.json(sanitized);
});
