  res.status(200).json({ status: 'ok' });
  // Never include versions, env names, internal IPs, etc.
});
```

---

#### 10. No Request Body Size Limit (OWASP A04)

Without `express.json()` configured with a size limit, a future POST route is vulnerable to payload-based DoS (sending gigabytes of JSON).

**Fix — configure a body size limit explicitly:**
```js
app.use(express.json({ limit: '10kb' }));      // Reject oversized JSON
app.use(express.urlencoded({ extended: true, limit: '10kb' }));
```

