Email addresses are returned directly. In real applications this commonly extends to passwords, tokens, or PII being over-exposed in API responses.

**Fix — explicitly whitelist returned fields:**
```js
app.get('/users', requireAuth, (req, res) => {
  const users = getAllUsers(); // your data source
  const safeUsers = users.map(({ id, name }) => ({ id, name }));
