## Finding 9 — 🟡 MEDIUM: No HTTPS Enforcement (OWASP A02)

**Problem:** The server listens on plain HTTP. All tokens, passwords, and PII travel in cleartext.

**Fix:**
```js
// Option A — terminate TLS at the app layer (useful for standalone deployments)
const https = require('https');
const fs    = require('fs');

const tlsOptions = {
  key:  fs.readFileSync(process.env.TLS_KEY_PATH),
  cert: fs.readFileSync(process.env.TLS_CERT_PATH),
};
https.createServer(tlsOptions, app).listen(443);

// Redirect HTTP → HTTPS
const http = require('http');
http.createServer((req, res) => {
  res.writeHead(301, { Location: `https://${req.headers.host}${req.url}` });
  res.end();
}).listen(80);

// Option B (recommended for production) — put a TLS-terminating reverse proxy
//   (nginx, AWS ALB, Cloudflare) in front and just ensure HSTS is set via Helmet.
```

---

## Finding 10 — 🔵 INFORMATIONAL: No `package.json` / Dependency Scanning (OWASP A06)

**Problem:** There is no `package.json` in the workspace, so dependency versions and vulnerability status are unknown. Outdated packages are the #1 source of known exploits.

**Recommendations:**
```bash
