### 🟠 Finding 8 — No Error Handling / Information Leakage (OWASP A09)

**Problem:** There is no global error handler. Unhandled errors will cause Express to send a default response that may include stack traces, file paths, or other internal details.

**Fix:** Add a structured error handler as the **last** middleware:

```js
// Generic error handler — must have 4 parameters for Express to recognize it
app.use((err, req, res, next) => {
  // Log the full error internally (use a proper logger like winston/pino in production)
  console.error({
    message: err.message,
    stack: err.stack,
    path: req.path,
    method: req.method,
  });

  // Never send internal details to the client
  const statusCode = err.status ?? err.statusCode ?? 500;
  res.status(statusCode).json({
    error: statusCode < 500 ? err.message : 'An internal error occurred.',
  });
});
```

