### 🟠 Finding 9 — No HTTPS Enforcement (OWASP A02)

**Problem:** The app has no mechanism to redirect HTTP to HTTPS or to set HSTS headers, leaving credentials and data vulnerable to interception in transit.

**Fix (application layer):** Helmet's HSTS header is a good start (enabled by `helmet()` in Finding 1). Additionally, add an HTTP→HTTPS redirect for direct Express deployments:

```js
// Redirect HTTP → HTTPS (if not behind a TLS-terminating proxy)
app.use((req, res, next) => {
  if (req.headers['x-forwarded-proto'] === 'http') {
    return res.redirect(301, `https://${req.headers.host}${req.url}`);
  }
  next();
});
```

> If you're behind a load balancer or reverse proxy (NGINX, AWS ALB), enforce TLS termination there and trust the `X-Forwarded-Proto` header.

