### The Key Rules, Regardless of Which Option You Choose

| Rule | Why |
|---|---|
| Never commit `.env` files | Git history is permanent; rotation is painful |
| Never write secrets back to `process.env` | Global, readable by any dependency |
| Never log secrets, even on error | Log aggregators are a common exfil path |
| Validate secrets exist at startup | Fail loudly rather than serve broken/insecure responses |
| Rotate secrets on any suspected exposure | Treat exposure as compromise |
| Use separate secrets per environment | A leaked dev secret must not work in production |

---

