## 🟡 Medium Severity Issues

### 7. No Centralised Error Handler (OWASP A09 – Security Logging & Monitoring Failures)

**Problem:** With no error handler, Express's default will dump stack traces — including file paths, library versions, and internal logic — directly to API consumers in development mode, and may silently swallow errors in production.

**Fix:**

```js
// ✅ Add as the LAST middleware, after all routes
app.use((err, req, res, next) => {
  const status = err.status || err.statusCode || 500;

  // Structured log for your monitoring system (never to the response)
  console.error({
    message: err.message,
    stack: err.stack,
    path: req.path,
    method: req.method,
    requestId: req.id,
  });

  // Never leak internals to the client
  res.status(status).json({
    error: status < 500 ? err.message : 'An unexpected error occurred',
  });
});
```

