## Finding 3 — 🟠 `/users` Exposes Raw PII with No Scoping
**OWASP A04:2021 – Insecure Design**

The `/users` endpoint returns all users with their emails in a single unauthenticated call. This is a classic **Broken Object Level Authorization (BOLA/IDOR)** setup. Even after auth is added, returning *all* users instead of scoping to the requester is a design flaw.

**Current code:**
```js
app.get('/users', (req, res) => {
  res.json([
    { id: 1, name: 'Alice', email: 'alice@example.com' },  // ← PII, unscoped
    { id: 2, name: 'Bob',   email: 'bob@example.com'  },
  ]);
});
```

**Fix — scope responses to the authenticated user and strip unnecessary PII:**
```js
app.get('/users/me', requireAuth, (req, res) => {
  // Return only the requesting user's own data
  const user = getUserById(req.auth.sub);  // req.auth populated by JWT middleware
  if (!user) return res.status(404).json({ error: 'User not found' });

  // Explicitly allowlist returned fields — never spread entire DB rows
  res.json({
    id:   user.id,
    name: user.name,
    // email: user.email  ← only include if the user explicitly needs it
  });
});

// Separate admin-only route for listing all users
app.get('/users', requireAuth, requireRole('admin'), (req, res) => {
  const users = getAllUsers().map(({ id, name }) => ({ id, name })); // strip PII
  res.json(users);
});
```

