## Finding 8 — 🟡 No HTTPS / TLS Enforcement
**OWASP A02:2021 – Cryptographic Failures**

The server listens on plain HTTP port 3000 with no TLS and no mechanism to redirect or reject insecure connections. Any credentials, tokens, or PII transmitted are exposed in plaintext.

**Fix — enforce HTTPS in application code and infrastructure:**
```js
// Option A: Terminate TLS in-process (good for simple deployments)
const https = require('https');
const fs    = require('fs');

const tlsOptions = {
  key:  fs.readFileSync(process.env.TLS_KEY_PATH),   // Never hard-code paths
  cert: fs.readFileSync(process.env.TLS_CERT_PATH),
};

https.createServer(tlsOptions, app).listen(443, () => {
  logger.info('HTTPS server running on port 443');
});

// Redirect all HTTP to HTTPS
const http = require('http');
http.createServer((req, res) => {
  res.writeHead(301, { Location: `https://${req.headers.host}${req.url}` });
  res.end();
}).listen(80);

// Option B (preferred in production): Terminate TLS at a reverse proxy
// (nginx, AWS ALB, Cloudflare) and enforce HSTS via Helmet (see Finding 1):
app.use(helmet.hsts({ maxAge: 31536000, includeSubDomains: true, preload: true }));
```

