### 3. HIGH — No Authentication or Authorization (OWASP A01: Broken Access Control)

**Problem:** `GET /users` returns a full user list with no authentication whatsoever. Any anonymous request to `http://your-server:3000/users` gets all user data. There is also no role-based access control (RBAC) framework in place — adding new routes will repeat this mistake.

**Fix:** Add JWT-based authentication middleware:

```bash
npm install jsonwebtoken express-jwt
```

```js
const { expressjwt: jwt } = require('express-jwt');

// Protect all routes except /health
