### Rules That Apply Regardless of Approach

| Rule | Why |
|---|---|
| Never log `process.env` wholesale | One `console.log(process.env)` leaks every secret to stdout/log aggregators |
| Never expose secrets in error messages | Stack traces sent to clients may contain env context |
| Never commit `.env` files | Git history is permanent — rotation won't help once it's in history |
| Rotate secrets on any suspected exposure | Treat a leaked secret as already compromised |
| Use a secret per environment | Dev/staging/prod secrets must be different values |
| Audit secret access | Secrets managers log who fetched what and when; `.env` files do not |

---

