config.validate(); // Crash immediately if config is broken
```

---

## 📋 Summary of Recommendations

| Concern | Recommendation |
|---|---|
| **No secrets exist yet** | Good time to build the right pattern before any are added |
| **Local development** | Use `.env` + `dotenv`, but **never commit** the file |
| **Production** | Use AWS Secrets Manager, GCP Secret Manager, Azure Key Vault, or HashiCorp Vault |
| **`.env` in git** | Add `.env*` to `.gitignore` immediately, and add a `.env.example` template |
| **Missing secrets at startup** | Validate all required env vars on boot and `process.exit(1)` if any are absent |
| **Secret rotation** | Design secret loading to support rotation without redeployment (Vault leases or AWS rotation handles this automatically) |

The bottom line: **the absence of any secrets infrastructure is itself the vulnerability** — it means secrets will inevitably be added ad-hoc (hardcoded, committed to git, or scattered across files) unless the right pattern is established now.

